# The tokens that secret-setup stores with secret-set, and that secret-check looks for.
# Each line is "NAME description". A company adds its tokens in config/zsh/companies/COMPANY/secrets.list.
# Remove the "#" from a line to need the token on each computer.
# Prefer a CLI login, such as "gh auth login", to a token. See SECRETS.md.

# GITHUB_TOKEN  a GitHub token, only for a tool that reads the variable. gh uses its own login.
# HF_TOKEN  a Hugging Face token, from https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# LINEAR_API_KEY  only for a computer with no Linear MCP server
# NOTION_TOKEN  only for a computer with no Notion MCP server
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN  only for a computer with no Slack MCP server
